Z||000000||Carrolles||08-02-2000||09:28 AM||||I looked at a pretty rough 85GT last night.  It has 113000 miles showing.  It has the following options and problems:<P>red (paint in not too bad condition)<BR>started right up with no problems and seems to shift fine (auto trans) and have decent power<BR>no sunroof<BR>tattered grey interior<BR>cracked dash<BR>shredded seats<BR>e-brake does not work<BR>exhaust crossover is broken at the flange to the front eshaust manifold<BR>nose is slightly pushed in due to deer strike (not noticable until you close the front hood and it binds on the fascia)<BR>rear hatch release does not work<BR>rear hatch is slightly pushed forward<BR>dogbone bracket is broken where it bolts to the manifold<BR>no egr tube<BR>Headlight bracket is broken (probably due to deer strike) neither goes up or down<BR>Power locks don't work<BR>power windows are very slow<BR>aftermarket speaker grills screwed on top of stock grills (looks like cr%p)<BR>driver side door drags badly<BR>tires are fair<BR>brakes seem to pull when applied (couldn't drive it too fast due to noise)<BR>driver side door interior panel is shot<BR>power mirrors don't work<BR>shocks and struts are probably shot<P>The owner is asking $600 but will take $500.<P>I am going to tell him that if he can't find a buyer I'll give him $300.  Could be a donor for a re-body.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-02-2000||09:37 AM||||I bought the Grape Ape ('85 GT) for $350 with a bad engine and lots of minor needs.  The only major thing I've done so far is the motor.  I drive it everyday and once on a 300 mile (round trip) excursion.  Everything else works other than minor things.  Mine even has new Pirelli tires and 15" aftermarket wheels.  <P>I would think that $500 is waaaaay too high and $300 is pushing it.  Just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||08-02-2000||01:29 PM||||What do you mean looks pretty rough. That sounds cherry compared to my 87GT! LOL, not really.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||08-17-2000||05:19 PM||||-UPDATE-<P>Well the kid called me and said he'd take the $300 I offered.  My wife and I drove the 35 miles to his house in my van just in case I had to tow it home.<P>It drove fine although loudly.<P>Looking at it in daylight it's not nearly as bad as I thought.  The body is straight and was repainted some time back.  The gray ground effects are now the same red as the rest of the car.  The paint is decent so I don't see repainting any time soon.<P>THe interior cleaned up nicely.  I still haven't peeled back the new seat covers (read cheap seat covers) but all the padding seems to be in the right places.<P>The crossover pipe is not broken.  The bolts are just loose and frozen.  I'll hit them with WD-40 or cut them off.<P>The power windows do work and after installing the missing ctsy fuse the power locks, power mirrors, trunk light, and reading lights now work.  The trunk release does not work yet.  I suspect either the switch is disconnected (it was loose in the dash) or the relay is bad/not connected.<P>I replaced the speaker grill covers with a spare set I had.  The dash speakers are new.  I don't know why he bolted the speaker support brackets to the top side of the Fiero covers.<P>The engine lid was just pushed all the way forward.  I loosened the bolts and aligned it.  Looks fine now.  The nose shows no sign of mis-alignment so far.  Maybe it healed.<P>The dash has a hole next to the right speaker grill.  It doesn't look too bad but I'll replace it eventually.<P>The kid replaced the driver side door hing pin and bushings and it colses ok now.  The door panel is missing the lip along the top edge that holds it to the door.  I'll look for one at the junk yards.  So far the only ones I've found have the manual mirror bezel.<P>The speedometer does not work.  I haven't looked at it yet to see if the speed sensor is connected.  It appears that the engine has been pulled before because the wiring is not arranged like new.<P>The torque strut is broken where it bolts to the head.  The support bracket that it mounts to is missing.  I got a replacement from Ed Parks with the bolt for $20.00.<P>I searched the junk yards the other day and found an 85SE.  The guy will sell me the entire headlight system for $50.00 and the seats for $35.00 for the pair.<P>As soon as I finish some needed maintenance on a few of my other cars I'll get to this one.<P>Take care,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
